# Riesz--Thorin: scalar analytic-family foundation

Riesz--Thorin is obtained by applying Hadamard's three-lines theorem to a
carefully constructed scalar analytic family of pairings.  Mathlib already
contains the complex-analytic theorem.  This module records a stable,
namespace-local interface to that result and its unit-strip specialization.

The module also proves the complex normed-space-valued analytic-family consequence:
if the operator norms on the two boundary lines are bounded, then the
operator norm at every point in the strip has the interpolated bound.  This
is the scalar-pairing/Hahn--Banach part of Riesz--Thorin.  Interpolating
between *different* `Lp` spaces additionally requires the usual analytic
input/output powers and their measurability and integrability verification;
that construction is deliberately not hidden behind this API.
